# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file in this repo is stored with LF endings, and `text=auto` keeps
# it that way: git normalizes on commit, and compares a working-tree file with
# its carriage returns stripped. An editor or archive tool that rewrites endings
# on disk therefore no longer shows up as a thousand phantom modified files, and
# can no longer sneak CRLF into a commit.
#
# That second part matters here. docs/runbooks/BYTE-CHECK.md guarantees repo
# artifacts are byte-identical to what is deployed; a stray CRLF commit would
# silently break that guarantee on the next hash comparison.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch the bytes.
*.woff2 -text
*.woff  -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.png   -text
*.webp  -text
*.ico   -text
*.pdf   -text
*.zip   -text
*.docx  -text
